_with_Eastern_Yosemite_Valley.jpg","dist_m":6,"width":640,"height":406,"license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","artist":"Thomas Wolf, www.foto-tw.de"}],"street":{"image_id":"818576849082547","username":"coljay72","captured_at":"2012-09-27","is_pano":false,"dist_m":5,"url":"https://www.mapillary.com/app/?pKey=818576849082547","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"id":"node/3331427773","name":"Grizzly Giant","kind":"attraction","lon":-119.60072,"lat":37.50355,"ele_m":1788.0,"wikidata":"Q5609795","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grizzly_Giant","tour":7,"summary":{"extract":"The Grizzly Giant is a massive giant sequoia located in Mariposa Grove within Yosemite National Park. Famous for its impressive size and age, the Grizzly Giant has been a symbol of the park since tourism began. The Grizzly Giant stands out with its enormous trunk, which is much larger than typical giant sequoias, and its unique, uneven branches shaped by centuries of weather and environmental factors. Its name comes from its imposing presence, reminiscent of a California grizzly bear.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grizzly_Giant","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","attribution":"Wikipedia"},"photos":[{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Yosemite_National_Park_%28CA%2C_USA%29%2C_Mariposa_Grove_of_Giant_Sequoias%2C_Grizzly_Giant_--_2022_--_2758.jpg/960px-Yosemite_National_Park_%28CA%2C_USA%29%2C_Mariposa_Grove_of_Giant_Sequoias%2C_Grizzly_Giant_--_2022_--_2758.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yosemite_National_Park_(CA,_USA),_Mariposa_Grove_of_Giant_Sequoias,_Grizzly_Giant_--_2022_--_2758.jpg","dist_m":5,"width":640,"height":427,"license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","artist":"Dietmar Rabich"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Yosemite_National_Park%2C_Wawona_area%2C_Grizzly_Giant_%287889406484%29.jpg/960px-Yosemite_National_Park%2C_W